@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] shared-review-session-is-production-state
Android and iOS MUST use this same review-session implementation, including Compose
state, task observation, saved results, file marks and commit selection. Native services
MUST enter through the clock, effects and tour-cache interfaces; this module MUST NOT
depend on Android services. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-review-state-belongs-to-source
An application-owned review cache MUST contain data for only its current opaque RPC
source. Server/account invalidation MUST clear cached reviews and active private session
state and cancel warming and observations. A late response MUST NOT restore data or
deliver callbacks/effects after that source changes. Cache keys MUST NOT retain raw
credentials. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS session/cache ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-review-route-recovers-after-source-change
Server/account invalidation MUST discard the entire private review route's remembered
state and give a route that remains mounted a fresh, usable session, even when Settings
or sign-in covers it. A replacement source MUST NOT inherit prior sheets, drafts or
saved child state. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS source-identity ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-review-opens-from-bounded-cache
An opened review MUST show its kept diff before waiting for a request and MUST join
its in-flight warm. The recent-review cache MUST retain at most twelve reviews and
warming MUST be bounded; the Inbox's top four remain the initial warm set. Source:
the existing ReviewSession policy, retained by Tavi's 21 Oct iOS reuse decision;
recording 16 Oct 13:06, 09:09 to 09:17 (O20; DESIGN.md rule 187).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-review-late-responses-match-view
Patches, saved work, file marks and task updates MUST match the current diff key,
head and commit selection before changing presentation state. An older task revision
MUST NOT replace a newer one. Source: the accepted 21 Oct iOS session/state plan and
the existing current-head patch and commit-selection guards.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-review-detach-keeps-server-work
Leaving a route MUST stop its local observation without cancelling remote AI work.
Only an explicit Cancel action MAY invoke the server's task-cancellation operation.
Source: the accepted 21 Oct iOS lifecycle plan and existing ReviewSession detach policy.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-review-task-outcomes-are-authoritative
A failed observation or unknown status MUST NOT become an authoritative failed or
successful task, outcome cue or completion callback. Only server-reported done, failed
or cancelled snapshots MAY settle a task; cancellation MUST remain silent. Source:
Tavi's 21 Oct notification expansion and the existing shared-ai-outcome-owned-task policy.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-review-invalid-source-is-actionable
An invalid saved server MUST open a load-error state without warming or exposing a
previous source's cached data. Invalid source namespaces MUST NOT retain URL userinfo.
Source: the accepted 21 Oct iOS session/state plan's source-identity boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-review-observation-reconnects
Interrupted or unfamiliar task observations MUST retain running work and retry with
cancellable, capped backoff. The existing progress line MUST say Reconnecting while
observation is interrupted. A route or identity change MUST cancel those retries without
cancelling remote work. Source: the accepted 21 Oct iOS lifecycle plan and the existing
rule that server tasks survive phone suspension.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-stack-is-a-sheet
A pull request in a stack says so under its title ("Stacked on #241"), and a tap opens
the Stack sheet with every layer top first down to the base branch, where a tap on
another layer opens it (DESIGN.md checklist 51).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] pr-stack-layer-reads-like-a-row
Every layer in the Stack sheet MUST show its place in the stack in the leading column
("2/3") and, under its title, the Inbox rows' meta line: its number and its author, then
Merged or Closed, checks and + and − ("I cannot see the user's name ... It's like its
missing the PR number (not the in-stack one; that one is there), and the username": Tavi,
17 Oct 20:13; rule 203). The server's stack carries each layer's author for it.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-overview-actions-belong-to-route
Overview action state MUST run at most one action at a time and retain a rejected
action's error for recovery. A confirmed action MUST refresh before its completion
callback. Route/account cancellation MUST NOT publish a success/failure cue, error or
completion callback for a response that arrives after invalidation. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 shared state/source ownership plan and the existing ReviewTopUi action policy.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-opens-at-once
A pull request opened from a row shows its title, number, author, branches and size in
the first frame, from what the row knew, before GitHub answers. There is no "Loading pull
request" page; parts still on their way are skeletons (rules 50, 51 and 128; J13, H29).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;product] pr-opening-never-jumps
While a pull request opens, its head is laid out in its final shape from the first frame
and values change in place: no skeleton that turns into a numbers row that pushes things
down, and no button label that steps through "Review changes", "Review 84 files" and
"Review 83 files" (recording 15 Oct 13:54, 09:58; K22; rule 69).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] pr-sticky-head-stays-solid
The head of the pull request page stays pinned while the page scrolls ("They're sticky
and they should be"), and what is pinned stays fully readable: its buttons MUST NOT turn
half transparent over the numbers and tabs, and nothing sits under the status bar
(recording 15 Oct 13:54, 01:36 to 03:03; K6).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] pr-title-is-whole
The title is a plain 26sp heading that wraps whole, never cut and never in a bubble
(rules 2 and 12). The one exception is the Overview's pinned head: once the page scrolls,
the title folds to one line and MAY end in an ellipsis, and it is whole again at rest
("ellipsis allowed", recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 20:34 to 21:03; N38, Tavi's decision).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-edit-in-place
On a pull request the person may edit, a tap on the title turns it into a field with the
caret where the finger landed; the text is underlined in the accent and the rest of the
page fades to a quarter; leaving it saves. There is no Edit button (rules 83 and 110; F20,
H34, H35). The description is edited on a sheet instead: a tap opens it in a proper text
field and leaving the sheet saves; the page never scrolls under it (Tavi, recording 15 Oct
15:37, 08:29 to 08:56; L13). The sheet MUST open with the cursor at the place in the text
the tap was over, never at its end ("it scrolls me all the way down instead of stopping
where I was gonna edit", recording 17 Oct 14:45, 01:51 to 01:59; Q3; rule 199).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-edit-blocks-the-page
While the title or description is being edited, a tap anywhere else only leaves the
field: nothing under it switches tab, opens or swipes (J17).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] pr-no-editing-others-pull-requests
When GitHub says the person cannot update the pull request, its title and description are
plain text: no field, no caret, no fade ("I should not be able to change the title or
change the description", recording 15 Oct 13:54, 09:58 to 10:42; K21).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-branch-copies-with-a-toast
A tap on the branch copies its name and shows a small toast ("Branch name copied"); the
pill keeps showing the branch and never turns into "Copied" (rule 83; F21).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] pr-branch-row-is-one-line
The branch row is head → base on one line. A long branch runs past the edge and the row
scrolls sideways, fading at the edge it can scroll toward; "…" is the last resort (rules
74 and 111; H31, J14).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;product] pr-summary-switch-is-not-a-pill
The author's description and the AI's summary are not switched by a pill ("I don't like
this"). When the text changes it fades, which he liked (recording 15 Oct 13:54, 10:07 to
10:20; K23). The switch is the link alone, "Show the AI summary" or "Show the
description", with no word naming the text above it (recording 16 Oct 09:50, 02:31 to
02:55; M6).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-commits-and-checks-are-sheets
Commits is not a tab: tapping Commits opens a sheet like Files, with a "Find a commit"
search and plain headings, and Checks is a sheet made the same way ("all of these
components are things that we use everywhere", recording 15 Oct 13:54, 13:25 to 14:03;
K29).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-commit-opens-its-diff
Tapping a commit opens the diff of that commit alone (or that diff in a sheet). It MUST
NOT put a "Viewing commit N of M" box on top of the Overview (recording 15 Oct 13:54,
10:48 to 11:18; K25).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-narrowed-view-shows-the-way-back
When the Diff shows part of the pull request (one commit, a range), it says so where the
reader already looks, with no box over the page: the Diff's file pill names the commit and
the Overview's Commits number reads just "3" (or "12–15") so it fits its cell, and opens the
Commits sheet whose first row "All commits" goes back (rule 80; F26). The pill says "Only
commit 4", never "Commit 4 of 8", which read like a page count (recording 15 Oct 15:37,
07:06 to 07:17; L11). Tavi's K25 replaced the pinned "Viewing commit" bar
(recording 15 Oct 13:54, 10:48 to 11:18).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] pr-tabs-are-light
The Overview's tabs are underline tabs with no counts and no box, easy to hit, and close
together from the start of the line, not spread across the width (K7, Tavi's call); they
never cut a label. While the tabs swipe, the gap between the pages is narrow, never a wide
empty band (rules 38, 54 and 91; recording 15 Oct 13:54, 02:20 to 02:38; K7).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] pr-tabs-are-side-by-side
The Overview's tabs sit side by side and move the whole width with the finger, both in
view while moving, with the underline drawn where the pages are on every frame. A drag
anywhere on the head (title, meta, numbers, tabs) moves them, except the branch row's own
scroll and a file row's swipe (rules 107 and 118; J15, J21).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion] pr-last-tab-has-no-empty-page
On the last tab a swipe toward the next carries on to the Diff or does not move; it never
drags the page into empty space (recording 15 Oct 13:54, 03:12 to 03:26; K8; rule 93).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-tabs-keep-their-place
Each of the Overview's tabs keeps its scroll and what is open while another is on
screen, and the head lifts with whichever tab is in view (rule 118; J9).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-files-fold-and-search
The files are grouped under fold headings on the Overview, and a fold is kept while the
pull request is open. Over 80 files every section starts folded. The Files sheet groups
them under the sheets' plain headings with nothing folded (M7), and has a search where a
row matches when every typed word is in it (rules 101 and 119).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] pr-counts-sit-side-by-side
The +N −N of a file row, a file section heading and the Files sheet sit side by side on
one line, as on Home, never stacked and never clipped (recording 15 Oct 13:54, 10:23 and
12:16 to 12:58; K24, K27).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] pr-file-row-swipes
A file row on the Overview swipes like a pull request row: right opens it, left marks it
reviewed (or not), a tap opens it and a hold opens its actions. Its checkbox sits on the
first line of text (rule 102; F44, F46).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-conversation-folds
Every comment in Conversation folds; a person's starts open and a bot's starts folded.
"commented" is never written, and the age and chevron line up at the right of every
header (rule 91; F72).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-conversation-narrows
When both people and bots spoke, chips narrow the Conversation to All, People or Bots
with their counts, and a narrowed list shows all of its comments (rule 129; J19).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-conversation-skips-the-description
Conversation MUST NOT show the pull request's description as its first comment: Summary
already shows it, so the tab starts with what was said after it, and one muted line says
so when nobody has commented ("the first comment is just the PR's description", recording
of 16 Oct 12:10, 15:44 to 16:01, N30, Tavi's decision).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-bots-are-githubs-word
People and Bots split on GitHub's own data: an author is a bot when the server marks it
(`bot`, from its GraphQL type `Bot`) or its login ends in "[bot]". The app MUST NOT keep a
list of bot names, so chatgpt-codex-connector, devin-ai-integration and github-actions are
bots and a person is never one for their name ("without banning names", recording of
16 Oct 12:10, 16:02 to 16:21, N31).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] pr-checks-read-cleanly
Checks lists failed first, then running, then passed; a row taps through to the check.
A check's name does not wrap into many lines, and the sheet's close button and its
heading keep the standard gap (rule 79; recording 15 Oct 13:54, 13:01 to 13:24; K28).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] pr-sheet-rows-in-cards
In the pull request's sheets the rows sit in the raised cards every other sheet uses,
one card under each heading, rows at least 60dp with whole titles (rule 79; J24, F27).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] pr-groups-say-a-shared-start-once
File groups in a row named "Prefix › Something" with the same Prefix are listed under one
line saying the Prefix, and each group's row says only the rest. Two group rows on the
Overview MUST NOT start with the same words ("Wayland capture producer" four times,
recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 17:41 to 18:02; N34). A group keeps its fold under its whole
name.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] pr-texts-never-stand-in-columns
Two texts MUST NOT sit side by side where one wraps into a narrow column beside the other.
A file row's whole path runs on after "Worth a look ·" and wraps under it, as one paragraph
("almost a rule I personally have", recording of 16 Oct 12:10, 19:49 to 20:16; N37).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-opens-current-text
Opening a pull request, coming back to it, or tapping a link to the one on screen MUST put
the title and description GitHub holds now in place of a kept copy as soon as the small
`pr-text` answer arrives, without waiting for the whole overview; a link to the page on
screen reads it again rather than doing nothing (Tavi, thread message 16 Oct 13:52, "the
description was not updated").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] pr-metadata-stays-one-line
The repository, number, author and age MUST remain on one line. Variable names MUST
yield at their ends while number and age retain their width (DESIGN.md rule 26;
repository review 15 Oct 2026, finding 13).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] ask-bar-rests-short
A page's Ask bar (the Overview, its opening page and the Tour) MUST rest as a short pill,
centred, that reads Ask, with no button. A tap opens it to the full width with the cursor
in its field and its button at the end; left with nothing typed, it goes short again
("let's not have this send button and let's just have like a shorter bar that says Ask.
And when you tap on it ... it kind of expands ... and then obviously compacts back
whenever you get out of that", recording 17 Oct 14:45, 02:26 to 03:19; Q5; rule 197).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] pr-description-written-rendered
The description sheet's field MUST read its Markdown rendered while it is typed, as
Obsidian's live preview does: headings and strong words heavier, emphasis slanted, code
in the code face, links in the link ink and a list's dash as a bullet, with the marks
folded away on every line but the cursor's. Every character MUST stay as typed, so what is
saved is the Markdown ("It is fine to let me do markdown, but just render it immediately,
basically. Something like Obsidian", recording 17 Oct 14:45, 02:00 to 02:25; Q4; rule 200).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] pr-number-opens-github
Tapping a pull request number in its metadata MUST open
https://github.com/{owner}/{repo}/pull/{number} in an external browser using an explicitly
selected package, bypassing Pully app-link capture. Commit, compare and posted-diff
metadata MUST NOT invent a PR link (Tavi, 20 Oct 2026: "Pressing on the PRs number should
open the PR on GitHub... Pully captures GitHub links... needs to not do that").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] pr-files-reviewed-strikethrough
In the Files bottom sheet, a file whose existing review state is Reviewed MUST strike
through its filename and folder path. Unreviewed and Changed files MUST remain unstruck;
the checkbox and existing review state remain the source of truth (Tavi, 20 Oct 2026
controls feedback).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] pr-lifecycle-is-visible
The pull request detail header MUST visibly say Merged or Closed when GitHub reports
that lifecycle, using the app's existing state ink and glyphs independently of check
results. A merge timestamp or an observed merged state MUST take precedence over an
open, closed or draft copy and MUST disable merge actions; a fresh known open overview
MAY replace a previously closed copy after reopening. Missing or unrecognized lifecycle
without terminal evidence MUST NOT be treated as open. A current diff's known state MUST
replace a cached overview's older state; lifecycle and same-PR link refreshes MUST update
the displayed status without a manual Refresh. A known lifecycle from the list MUST
survive the opening preview (Tavi, 20 Oct 2026: "On PRs that have already been merged,
we have no indication that they've been merged").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product;security] shared-overview-requires-real-host-services
Both hosts MUST render the same production Overview, Conversation, metadata and reading
sheets. Clipboard, external GitHub/browser destinations and lifecycle MUST use the one
required native actions service. Inline-edit Back MUST cancel the field before the
shared route pops, through the host's existing Back dispatcher; iOS MUST NOT install a
second competing edge recognizer. A host without that dispatcher MUST keep text editing
unavailable even when the server grants permission. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026
shared Overview and native-service plan, preserving pr-edit-in-place and pr-number-opens-github.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture;security] shared-overview-capabilities-precede-ai-actions
A host MUST declare unavailable AI reading, setup and paid actions before exposing
Overview controls or issuing their requests. Supported AI content MUST use the actual
production renderer with citations, task guards and complete outcomes; an empty or
no-op content provider MUST NOT claim support. Android MUST retain its current Brief,
AI summary, file note and findings renderers until those implementations move to common
code. A host without them MUST say that kept AI results are unavailable and MUST NOT
start invisible work. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 ordered extraction and explicit
OverviewAiContent decision; full native AI reading remains pending that renderer move.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-overview-commit-days-use-local-calendar
Commit-day groups MUST retain their existing contiguous order and Today, Yesterday,
English weekday/date labels in the device's time zone. A missing commit date MUST
follow the preceding group or read Undated when first. Android MUST retain its current
java.time formatter; native calendar adaptation MUST NOT change the commit indices or
selection behavior. Source: existing CommitsSheet/commitDays behavior retained by
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse decision.
